{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3095-750e-b5b9-92ff1235377b","id":"01a1a640-7d66-77e9-bc70-1b06785c705b","idempotency_key":"f24a22b012ef68ef74427ed56c60967452d48a8aea12a54636d16a8fa9bf1774","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:06Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-af11","note":"scripts/check_all.sh runs cargo test --workspace and --workspace --all-features, so every fixture above runs in the one command.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-5774/i-af11"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3095-750e-b5b9-92ff1235377b","id":"01a1a640-7d82-71d4-8203-cf1d96b6f5a5","idempotency_key":"f4c358443463f646b07737be3dd02c831393ab410ac19a731f69cd0e7ac2ecdb","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:06Z","payload":{"note":"All four. crates/rbc-db/tests/foundation.rs is the fixture file: a database stamped at version 3 that opens, migrates, keeps its game and moves its session into legacy_sessions; a workspace holding several boards where each counts its own revisions and a stale revision is refused naming the current one; a locked board that refuses a write and offers a copy which then takes it; a study keeping chapters in order, reordering without loss, publishing a version and recording per-chapter progress; and a session with its transcript surviving a close and reopen. The CDP half is already committed as cdp_cross_board.js (three boards through the strip, the AI target marker, the off-screen badge, the left-rail tree), and scripts/check_all.sh runs both test profiles so the fixtures are in the one command. Two mistakes of mine were corrected by writing these: publishing a study after add_chapter expects the version add_chapter already bumped, and hand-writing a v3 games table only proved my guess matched my own query - the fixture now imports through the real path and labels the database v3, which is the part the migration acts on.","target":"t-5774"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
